# discovery-sim

Local A2A 1.0 agents (chatbot, bank, payment) with MCP-backed bank and payment tools over a synthetic ledger.

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Run agents

```bash
discovery-sim agents
```

Default ports: chatbot `8001`, bank `8002`, payment `8003`.

## Run attack episodes (no HTTP servers required)

```bash
discovery-sim run --episodes 100 --seed 42 --out data/runs/42
```

First N episodes can use a **real LM Studio** planner (benign only; wrong plans are dropped):

```bash
export LMSTUDIO_MODEL=your-model
discovery-sim run --episodes 20 --llm-samples 5 --seed 42 --out data/runs/llm5
```

Writes `episodes.jsonl`, `examples.jsonl`, `laya_train.jsonl`, `questions.json`, and `baseline.json`. Multi-step scenarios share one ledger per episode; each example includes `prior_calls`, `trusted`, and `ledger_snapshot` in the state.

## Tests

```bash
pytest
```
